# ~/.vfg/config: every Everhear setting on your PC, KEY=value, mode 600.
# toolkit/install.sh copies this file there. The vfg toolkit, the brain, bridge/deploy/*.sh,
# jev/deploy.sh, installer/publish.sh and lib/py all read it.
# An environment variable of the same name wins. An empty value means the default.
# No secret goes here: the key's path only, never the key.

# --- You ---
# Your Minecraft name: the server's owner. Only the owner may ask for op, bans, the
# whitelist, stopping the server and the like; the brain reads it. Required.
VFG_OWNER=

# --- The EC2 box ---
# The box's public IP or DNS name; new each time the instance is launched or started. Required.
VFG_SSH_HOST=
# Default: ec2-user
VFG_SSH_USER=
# Path to the SSH private key of VFG_KEY_PAIR, e.g. ~/.ssh/everhear.pem (only the path is read). Required.
VFG_SSH_KEY=
# The AWS region the box and the installer bucket live in. Default: us-east-2
VFG_AWS_REGION=
# Default: m7i.xlarge
VFG_INSTANCE_TYPE=
# The EC2 key pair ec2.sh launch puts on the box. Default: everhear
VFG_KEY_PAIR=
# Where ec2.sh retire keeps the world's backups and deploy.sh provision --restore
# finds them. Default: ~/everhear/backups
VFG_BACKUP_DIR=
# Set it to true once you have read and accepted Minecraft's EULA
# (https://aka.ms/MinecraftEULA); deploy.sh provision needs it for a new world.
VFG_ACCEPT_EULA=
# A .env file, mode 600, outside any repo, holding the box's secrets (TYPESAFE_API_KEY, and
# VFG_CLIENT_TOKEN to keep one token across boxes). deploy.sh provision and deploy.sh env send
# those names to /opt/vfg/.env; any other key in the file stays on this PC.
# Default: ~/.vfg/box.env
VFG_BOX_ENV=

# --- The installer link (installer/publish.sh) ---
# The private S3 bucket; publish.sh makes one and writes its name here on the first run.
VFG_INSTALL_BUCKET=
# The address players join. Default: VFG_SSH_HOST
VFG_INSTALL_ADDRESS=
# Where the built mod jar is. Default: client-mod/build/libs in this repo
VFG_CLIENT_JAR_DIR=

# --- The vfg toolkit ---
# What vfg say puts first, in aqua. Default: "[AI] " (quote it to keep the space).
VFG_CHAT_PREFIX=
# Where brain/run, actions/, engine/library/ and made/ are. Default: the repo the toolkit is in
VFG_REPO=
# The bridge's folder on EC2. Default: /opt/vfg
VFG_REMOTE_VFG=
# The Minecraft server's folder on EC2. Default: /opt/mc
VFG_REMOTE_MC=
# Most lines vfg watch replays after a gap. Default: 100
VFG_WATCH_CATCHUP=
# The valve: most lines vfg watch prints in any minute. Default: 120
VFG_WATCH_MAX_PER_MIN=
# The ssh binary. Default: ssh
VFG_SSH=
# Seconds vfg engine start and vfg action run engine_start wait for a one-off scenario's
# result, 0 to 30. Default: 15
VFG_ENGINE_START_WAIT_S=
# The model of an incantation's alias call (vfg engine bind), through OpenRouter; off for none
# (the code's aliases alone). Default: google/gemini-3.8-flash
VFG_INCANT_ALIAS_MODEL=
# Where vfg made save keeps its saves of made/<server>/. Default:
# /var/home/jm/Documents/EverHear/Internal/made
VFG_MADE_ARCHIVE=

# --- The brain (brain/run; vfg brain start runs it) ---
# The file holding your OpenRouter API key alone, mode 600; lib/py's structured() reads
# it, and the implementers on openrouter. OPEN_ROUTER_API in the environment wins over the file.
# Default: ~/.vfg/openrouter.key
VFG_OPENROUTER_KEY=
# The OpenRouter model of every step of the brain's loops, and its reasoning effort: off, or an
# effort (low). Defaults: deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash, low
VFG_BRAIN_MODEL=
VFG_BRAIN_REASONING=
# OpenRouter providers to try first for the brain's steps, in that order, fallbacks allowed, so a
# loop's steps keep one host's cache; none lets OpenRouter choose.
# Default: together,coreweave,parasail
VFG_BRAIN_PROVIDERS=
# Seconds one step's call may take, its resend and retries included.
# Default: 120, or 60 with VFG_BRAIN_REASONING off
VFG_BRAIN_TIMEOUT_S=
# A loop's budget: its steps for its first line, and as many more for each line added; never
# past the cap, where its last step replies or hands off and it is deleted; and the seconds from
# its creation in which a line added takes an ended loop up again (0: never). Defaults: 10, 20, 120
VFG_LOOP_STEPS=
VFG_LOOP_CAP=
VFG_LOOP_TAKE_UP_S=
# The conversation agent, which answers every line to the AI at once and hands off a line that
# needs something done: its model, reasoning and providers, tried first in that order.
# Defaults: deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash, off, together,coreweave,parasail
VFG_RESPOND_MODEL=
VFG_RESPOND_REASONING=
VFG_RESPOND_PROVIDERS=
# Seconds one conversation agent call may take, its retries included, before the line is
# handed off with no reply. Default: 20
VFG_RESPOND_TIMEOUT_S=
# The router, which picks who does the work a hand-off asks for. While its reasoning is off, the
# conversation agent's line to a hand-off is held until the router has answered: one line per ask.
# Defaults: deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash, off, together,coreweave,parasail
VFG_ROUTER_MODEL=
VFG_ROUTER_REASONING=
VFG_ROUTER_PROVIDERS=
# Seconds one router call may take, its retries included, before the line goes to a new loop.
# Default: 30, or 60 with VFG_ROUTER_REASONING not off
VFG_ROUTER_TIMEOUT_S=
# One turn per player: the lines that may wait for it (one more is turned away, told so
# privately), and the seconds a turn waits for the rows it wrote to come back before the
# next starts (0: no wait). Defaults: 3, 3
VFG_TURN_WAITING=
VFG_TURN_SETTLE_S=
# Hours of the feed the brain reads as its context; vfg context's default. Default: 6
VFG_BRAIN_HISTORY_HOURS=6
# Every how many minute-blocks of the conversation a call marks for the prompt cache
# (a brain step and the router: at most two marks; the conversation agent: three). Default: 5
VFG_BRAIN_CHECKPOINT=
# The brain's folder: brain.log, brain.pid, lock and the command references. The tasks are
# in the box's vfg.db, written only by the brain.
# Default: $VFG_HOME/brain
VFG_BRAIN_DIR=

# --- Implementers (started by the brain, on DeepSeek V4.1 Flash) ---
# The harness an implementer runs in: claude-code or opencode. Default: claude-code
VFG_IMPL_HARNESS=
# Where it reaches the model: deepseek (DeepSeek's own API, its key DEEPSEEK_API_KEY in the
# brain's environment, never here), openrouter (the OpenRouter key above), or anthropic (Haiku
# 5.5 on your Claude subscription, Claude Code only, untested).
# Default: deepseek when DEEPSEEK_API_KEY is set, else openrouter
VFG_IMPL_PROVIDER=
# The model. Default: the provider's: deepseek-flash, deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash or
# claude-haiku-5-5 (VFG_IMPLEMENTER_MODEL is read when this is empty)
VFG_IMPL_MODEL=
# The provider's Claude-compatible address. Default: https://api.deepseek.com/anthropic or
# https://openrouter.ai/api; none for anthropic
VFG_IMPL_BASE_URL=
# On openrouter: the providers every request tries first, in order, and those it never uses,
# comma-separated, fallbacks allowed. Each keeps its own prompt cache, so a run that moves
# between them misses it; none empties a list. Together first, the fastest.
# Defaults: together,digitalocean,ionstream and venice,morph,relace
VFG_IMPL_OR_ORDER=
VFG_IMPL_OR_IGNORE=
# How hard the model thinks, on every provider and harness: off, low, high or max (medium is
# read as high; anything else stops the brain with an error). DeepSeek's own scale puts low,
# high and max at 50, 75 and 100 of 100, as DigitalOcean and Ionstream do through OpenRouter;
# Together puts them at 25, 50 and 100. Then the model requests a run may make (warned 5
# before the cap) and the minutes it may run (warned 1 before), past which it is stopped and its
# task failed. Defaults: high, 100, 20
VFG_IMPL_EFFORT=
VFG_IMPL_MAX_TURNS=
VFG_IMPLEMENTER_MINUTES=

# --- The server's content and the actions (vfg engine, vfg action run) ---
# The server this PC drives, and the name of its folder under made/, where what its
# implementers make (made/<server>/content/ and tests/) is kept apart from the library,
# engine/library/. Default: main
VFG_SERVER=
# Seconds the brain waits for a vfg action run, when the action sets no timeout_s of its own;
# past it (and 10 s of grace) the action is "failed": it may still have happened. Default: 20
VFG_DISPATCH_ACTION_TIMEOUT_S=

# --- The router (vfg route) and the implementers' cache ---
# Seconds vfg route waits for Jev before it picks by words instead. Default: 3
VFG_ROUTE_TIMEOUT_S=
# What loads an example class for an implementer (Jev's runs_it and close together), from 0
# to 1. Default: 0.3
VFG_ROUTE_LOAD=
# How long an implementer's prompt cache lives on the anthropic provider, 5m or 1h (DeepSeek
# caches on its own). An hour doubles the price of every cache write.
# VFG_SUBAGENT_CACHE_TTL is read when this is empty. Default: 5m
VFG_IMPL_CACHE_TTL=

# --- The test server (vfg test) ---
# Where vfg test runs an implementer's test: a second Minecraft server with Carpet's fake players,
# never the live one; livetest runs it there on an engine of its own. Empty or box: the live box's own, beside the live server, /opt/vfg-test and
# /opt/mc-test (VFG_REMOTE_VFG and VFG_REMOTE_MC + "-test"; on realmc, <name>/vfg-test and
# <name>/mc-test), which deploy.sh testserver makes (provision and deploy.sh too). none: no test
# server (vfg test exits 3). Anything else: a file of a test box's settings, KEY=value lines as
# this file has them, of which VFG_SSH, VFG_SSH_HOST, VFG_SSH_USER, VFG_SSH_KEY, VFG_REMOTE_VFG
# and VFG_REMOTE_MC are read over these (a key it leaves out is the live box's: leave out the
# host, whose IP changes with each relaunch, for a test server on the live box). Default: box
VFG_TEST_BOX=
# Seconds a test may run before it is stopped, 5 to 600. Default: 60
VFG_TEST_TIMEOUT_S=
# Seconds a test waits for the tests before it on the test server (one runs at a time) before
# vfg test gives up with exit 5, 0 to 3600; at most what a vfg test's 590 s leave once its own
# --timeout, VFG_TEST_WARM_GRACE (30 s), one VFG_TEST_BOOT_S and overhead are counted, always
# leaving at least 30 s here; a --timeout too large for even that is refused.
# Default: 300
VFG_TEST_QUEUE_S=
# Seconds the test server may take to answer RCON after vfg test restarts it (for a fresh world,
# or because it was down) before vfg test gives up with exit 5, 5 to 600. Default: 120
VFG_TEST_BOOT_S=
# How a test is kept from the live server: auto (a transient systemd unit, sudo -n systemd-run,
# else systemd-run --user, else a plain process, said in its output), system, user or none.
# Default: auto
VFG_TEST_SANDBOX=
